     "explanation": "The casting (restructuring) belonged to the playwright; the performance belongs to Priya. Playing the smaller part fully is not submission — it is the refusal to let externals set her standard, and it keeps the only thing that was always hers: her craft. Minimal effort is the reciprocity trap from Enchiridion 30 (their bad conduct rewriting her role), and performative resentment makes her excellence conditional on recognition. She remains free to seek a new job — in role, while playing this one well.",
